IndeProtoHub LLP Individual Contributor License Agreement (CLA)
Thank you for your interest in contributing to software, documentation, or other materials made available by IndeProtoHub LLP ("Company", "we", "us").

In order to clarify the intellectual property rights in contributions of software and documentation submitted to our projects, IndeProtoHub LLP must have a Contributor License Agreement ("CLA") on file that has been accepted by each contributor. This agreement protects both you and IndeProtoHub LLP, and ensures that the project and its derivatives can be maintained, adapted, and distributed without licensing conflicts.

Please read this document carefully before signing or submitting contributions.

1. Definitions
"You" (or "Contributor"): The individual copyright owner or legal entity authorized by the copyright owner that is entering into this Agreement with IndeProtoHub LLP.

"Contribution": Any original work of authorship, including any code modifications, enhancements, bug fixes, patches, documentation, or other intellectual property, submitted by You to IndeProtoHub LLP for inclusion in, or documentation of, any product, software, or project owned or managed by IndeProtoHub LLP.

"Submit" (or "Submitted"): Any form of electronic, verbal, or written communication sent to IndeProtoHub LLP or its representatives, including but not limited to submissions via GitHub/GitLab pull requests, commit histories, code reviews, issue tracking systems, or email lists.

